{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20184",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.13,
      "end_seconds": 4.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.1,
      "end_seconds": 10.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.75,
      "end_seconds": 18.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got cramps in my calves at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.28,
      "end_seconds": 22.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.69,
      "end_seconds": 26.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "It's been three weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.55,
      "end_seconds": 34.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.05,
      "end_seconds": 62.29,
      "duration_seconds": 26.24,
      "text": "I notice it more with lying in bed. I'd call it moderate. It's a few times a day. And tingling in my feet, too. As for tingling in my feet, it happens a couple of times a week. There's a dull ache after the cramp as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.9,
      "end_seconds": 67.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.09,
      "end_seconds": 72.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I'd give it a four, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.46,
      "end_seconds": 75.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.49,
      "end_seconds": 90.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.3,
      "end_seconds": 108.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 15, pulse 70, temp 36.5 degrees, blood pressure 109 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.41,
      "end_seconds": 110.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.5,
      "end_seconds": 114.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Okay, I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.08,
      "end_seconds": 120.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.87,
      "end_seconds": 122.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.28,
      "end_seconds": 125.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.63,
      "end_seconds": 151.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "Both calves are soft and not tender, and the pulses at your feet are good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.67,
      "end_seconds": 158.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Did you notice any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.5,
      "end_seconds": 163.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Not at all, no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.68,
      "end_seconds": 170.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Alright, any swelling of the legs, chest pain or back pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.12,
      "end_seconds": 176.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.29,
      "end_seconds": 182.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.14,
      "end_seconds": 185.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.92,
      "end_seconds": 191.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.92,
      "end_seconds": 195.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.2,
      "end_seconds": 210.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.25,
      "end_seconds": 228.27,
      "duration_seconds": 17.02,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I hardly move around during the day. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.72,
      "end_seconds": 236.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.08,
      "end_seconds": 248.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.39,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years. Yes, diabetes. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.69,
      "end_seconds": 255.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Yes. Okay, I can see high blood pressure in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.82,
      "end_seconds": 271.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.23,
      "end_seconds": 277.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Mm, uh, just a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.7,
      "end_seconds": 281.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.04,
      "end_seconds": 293.91,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "It's valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure. It's glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. It's clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.44,
      "end_seconds": 297.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "When did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.74,
      "end_seconds": 305.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "About about a month. Magnesium tablets. I take it at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.02,
      "end_seconds": 309.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.49,
      "end_seconds": 312.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "For about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.35,
      "end_seconds": 319.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.86,
      "end_seconds": 325.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "I'm allergic to naproxen, I get stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.03,
      "end_seconds": 342.88,
      "duration_seconds": 14.85,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it points towards night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause. I'd also keep a low salt level or low magnesium in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.79,
      "end_seconds": 346.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.15,
      "end_seconds": 361.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.67,
      "end_seconds": 383.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.72,
      "text": "I'm going to order a vitamin level, for tingling feet. Keep well hydrated through the day. See me again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.58,
      "end_seconds": 386.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I can manage that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.88,
      "end_seconds": 395.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.43,
      "end_seconds": 398.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.23,
      "end_seconds": 400.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}